<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances rise in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances rise in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances fell in the week that ended November 6, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				    Wk to Nov 6   Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  27.33   +0.229    +0.487</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     9.04   +5.795    +1.307</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	465.78   +0.671   +10.368</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 147.30   -4.600   -18.800</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  33.46   +3.773    +5.032</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>Chartered bank assets		  Sept	     Aug</p>
<p>  Net foreign currency		-12.32	   -11.24</p>
<p>  Canadian dollar		     653.15	   640.42</p>
<p>  Total Canadian liquid assets    102.95	   102.78</p>
<p>					 Sept 96     Aug 96    Sept 95</p>
<p>M1					 63.97	63.50     58.36</p>
<p>M2					390.60     389.11    382.89</p>
<p>M3					484.49     482.42    466.11</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars</p>
</text>
